---
// Privacy & Local-First Architecture Component
---

<section class="privacy-section" id="privacy" aria-label="Privacy Guarantees">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="privacy-inner card card-elevated">
      <div class="privacy-content">
        <span class="section-label">Local-First Architecture</span>
        <h2 class="section-title">Your reading belongs to you</h2>
        <p class="privacy-lead">
          Lirune keeps your library and reading experience on your device. We believe software should respect human attention and privacy without conditional fine print.
        </p>

        <div class="privacy-grid">
          <div class="privacy-box">
            <div class="box-icon">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="box-title">Zero Accounts or Tracking</h3>
            <p class="box-desc">
              You never need an email, phone number, password, or third-party login to read your books. We collect zero analytics, behavioral events, or telemetry.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="privacy-box">
            <div class="box-icon">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="12" cy="5" rx="9" ry="3"/><path d="M21 12c0 1.66-4 3-9 3s-9-1.34-9-3"/><path d="M3 5v14c0 1.66 4 3 9 3s9-1.34 9-3V5"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="box-title">Local-Only Storage</h3>
            <p class="box-desc">
              Your book files, bookmarks, reading percentages, and personal notes remain in sandboxed device storage (IndexedDB on Windows, SQLite on Android).
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="privacy-box">
            <div class="box-icon">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><line x1="1" y1="1" x2="23" y2="23"/><path d="M16.72 11.06A10.94 10.94 0 0 1 19 12.55"/><path d="M5 12.55a10.94 10.94 0 0 1 5.17-2.39"/><path d="M10.71 5.05A16 16 0 0 1 22.58 9"/><path d="M1.42 9a15.91 15.91 0 0 1 4.7-2.88"/><path d="M8.53 16.11a6 6 0 0 1 6.95 0"/><line x1="12" y1="20" x2="12.01" y2="20"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="box-title">Permanent Zero Network Permissions (Android)</h3>
            <p class="box-desc">
              Lirune Android explicitly strips the <code>android.permission.INTERNET</code> permission in release APKs, making network calls physically impossible by the OS.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="privacy-box">
            <div class="box-icon">
              <svg width="22" height="22" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15v4a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2v-4M17 8l-5-5-5 5M12 3v12"/></svg>
            </div>
            <h3 class="box-title">Self-Sovereign Data Backups</h3>
            <p class="box-desc">
              Export your entire reading history, annotations, and collections into a single JSON file anytime, and restore it anywhere without vendor lock-in.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="privacy-note">
          <p>
            <em>Clarification on Web Hosting:</em> This website itself is statically hosted on Google Firebase Hosting with standard HTTP delivery logs. However, the Lirune desktop and mobile applications operate strictly offline and do not connect to this website, Firebase, or any analytics servers during reader execution.
          </p>
          <a href="/privacy" class="link-privacy">Read our complete Privacy Architecture documentation →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .privacy-section {
    padding-top: var(--sp-12);
    padding-bottom: var(--sp-16);
  }

  .privacy-inner {
    padding: clamp(var(--sp-8), 4vw, var(--sp-12));
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }

  .privacy-lead {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    max-width: 760px;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-10);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .privacy-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: var(--sp-6);
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-10);
  }

  .privacy-box {
    background: var(--bg-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-radius: var(--r-lg);
    padding: var(--sp-6);
  }

  .box-icon {
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: var(--r-md);
    background: var(--accent-subtle);
    color: var(--accent-text);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-4);
  }

  .box-title {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    margin-bottom: var(--sp-2);
  }

  .box-desc {
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .box-desc code {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
    padding: 2px 4px;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent-chrome);
  }

  .privacy-note {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
    padding-top: var(--sp-6);
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--sp-3);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  .privacy-note p {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  .link-privacy {
    color: var(--accent-chrome);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .link-privacy:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
